From 2d77bf4629e64105a4b7b2b78ca4f6f7f8448414 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 14:24:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www/rc: remove AdGuard everywhere - menu, DNS presets,
 AiBoard cards, SDN hooks

Field ask: users do not want a third-party data collector present even inert
(the removed privacy-policy text itself stated data is collected by ADGUARD
SOFTWARE LIMITED). Removed all three surfaces:
- AdGuard DNS (Parental Controls tab + ADGUARDDNS_UI page set + menuTree
  entries in all six variants + rwd widget + state.js + dashboard hooks)
- AdGuard presets in DNS Director / DoT lists (DNSDirector.asp, DNS_List.json,
  dot-servers.json, web.c label rows; misc.c server rows blanked in place so a
  stale stored mode cannot read out of bounds)
- AdGuard Home + AdGuard DNS cards in AiBoard (registry, urlMap, install hook)
- SDN per-profile AdGuard machinery force-disabled (support flag hardwired
  false; the isSupport token lives in the closed priv_webapi.o prebuilt)
- RTCONFIG_ADGUARDDNS Kconfig stanza + dead config_base symbol dropped; the
  Makefile keeps the RWD_UI/SDN asset installs (MULTILAN path covers them)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
